      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the possibly preferred battery separators described herein</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">may exhibit a total thickness of less than about 30  ⁇ m, less than about 25  ⁇ m, less than about 20  ⁇ m, less than about 16  ⁇ mm, less than about 15  ⁇ m, less than about 14  ⁇ m, or less than about 10  ⁇ m, less than about 9  ⁇ m, less than about 8  ⁇ m, or less than about 6  ⁇ m (depending on the number of layers) and may surprisingly exhibit increased strength performance, as defined by reduced splittiness or reduced propensity to split, when compared to known battery separators of the same (or greater) thickness, especially when compared to known dry process battery separators of the same (or greater) thickness.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0016">
      </li>
      <li itemprop="definitions" itemscope repeat>
        <span itemprop="subject">the improvement in splitting or splittiness</span>
        <span itemprop="definition">may be quantified by a test method disclosed herein as Composite Splittiness Index (CSI) and the novel or improved separators described herein may have an improvement in the CSI, and also may exhibit improved Gurley as well as other improvements, such as improved puncture strength and so forth.</span>
        <meta itemprop="num_attr" content="0016">
